IMPORTANT CORRECTION TO PRELIMINARY STAGE20 INTERPRETATION
The three-argument call seen in IOSkywalkTxSubmissionQueue::packetSubmission is IOSkywalkQueryFreeSpaceHandler, not IOSkywalkTxSubmissionQueueAction. The TX submission action is five arguments as declared by the SDK and used by this project. The previous Stage20 note that labelled the action as three arguments was incorrect and has been corrected in stage20-private-skywalk-abi-discovery.sh.

RETURN SEMANTICS FROM SUPPLIED 24H32 DISASSEMBLY
RX submission action: callback EAX is added to the RX ring index; treat as a bounded ring-entry count.
RX completion action: callback EAX is consumed by enqueuePacketsForNetworking/enqueuePacketsForKPipe; treat as a bounded enqueue count.
TX completion action: callback EAX is passed to completePackets; treat as a bounded completion count.
TX submission action: its action call-site and return-value semantics are not yet independently proven in this review. Do not confuse it with the query-free-space handler, whose available-space output is written through UInt32 *outSpace.

CURRENT FAIL-CLOSED SOURCE RETURNS
TX submission action currently returns kIOReturnBadArgument for validation failures and kIOReturnNotReady when no handoff is implemented.
TX completion, RX submission, and RX completion actions currently return kIOReturnNotReady.
Those error constants must not be returned from callbacks whose EAX result is interpreted as a packet/ring count. The exact no-progress return and bounds must be implemented only after completing the TX submission action audit; the safe no-progress behavior for count-consuming call sites is zero.
